{
  $schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
  extends: ["github>openbunny/.github"],

  // The DCO check gates every pull request on a sign-off trailer that matches the
  // commit author, and Renovate authors its own commits. Without this its branches
  // can never go green, which is what stalled the whole queue.
  commitBody: "Signed-off-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
  description: [
    "Four holdbacks live below. allowedVersions drops a blocked update silently, so",
    "the dashboard is turned back on here, against the org preset, to give every",
    "hold one visible place and its 'closes when' a reason to be re-read.",
  ],
  dependencyDashboard: true,
  packageRules: [
    {
      description: [
        "HOLDBACK: Node stays on the 24 LTS line.",
        "openbunny/theme cannot follow to 26. The @types/node that ships with 26 no",
        "longer accepts string | undefined for assert.ok's message argument, and two",
        "call sites in its tests/tokens.test.ts pass exactly that, so its typecheck",
        "fails. theme, react and fiona.sm build on each other and should sit on one",
        "Node line; a major runtime bump also changes the npm version and the",
        "provenance environment that publish runs in. Nothing here is known to break",
        "on 26 -- the hold is about moving the three repositories together.",
        "Node 24 is LTS and fully supported, so waiting costs nothing.",
        "Closes when: theme coerces those two assert.ok messages and goes green on 26.",
      ],
      matchDatasources: ["node-version", "docker"],
      matchPackageNames: ["node"],
      allowedVersions: "<26",
    },
    {
      description: [
        "This package is published, so its peer ranges are a contract with consumers.",
        "The org preset sets rangeStrategy: pin globally, and pin reaches",
        "peerDependencies too: it would rewrite `react: ^19.3.0` to one exact version",
        "and conflict with every consumer on another 19.x. widen is what Renovate's",
        "own :pinAllExceptPeerDependencies preset does for peers. dependencies and",
        "devDependencies stay pinned.",
      ],
      matchDepTypes: ["peerDependencies"],
      rangeStrategy: "widen",
    },
    {
      description: [
        "One bun version is written in three places: packageManager and engines.bun",
        "in package.json, and bun in mise.toml. The npm and mise managers reach them",
        "separately, so ungrouped each opens its own pull request for one upgrade.",
        "openbunny/fiona.sm had exactly that split before it was grouped there.",
      ],
      matchPackageNames: ["bun"],
      groupName: "bun",
    },
    {
      description: [
        "@vitest/coverage-v8 declares a peer on the exact vitest version it ships",
        "alongside, so ungrouped the two arrive as separate pull requests and each",
        "one leaves the peer range unsatisfied. Neither can go green alone.",
      ],
      matchPackageNames: ["vitest", "@vitest/coverage-v8"],
      groupName: "vitest",
    },
    {
      description: [
        "react and react-dom are released as a pair, and react-dom's peer range on",
        "react is floored at its own version: react-dom 19.3.1 wants react ^19.3.1,",
        "so arriving alone it is unsatisfiable against react 19.3.0. The two @types",
        "packages track the same major.",
      ],
      matchPackageNames: [
        "react",
        "react-dom",
        "@types/react",
        "@types/react-dom",
      ],
      groupName: "react",
    },
    {
      description: [
        "next and eslint-config-next are published from one repository at one",
        "version. next is a devDependency here only so eslint-config-next resolves,",
        "so the two are meaningless apart.",
      ],
      matchPackageNames: ["next", "eslint-config-next"],
      groupName: "next",
    },
    {
      description: [
        "HOLDBACK: the ubuntu runner label stays on 24.04.",
        "ubuntu-26.04 is generally available, but actionlint recognises it in no",
        "release, so openbunny/theme holds it back to keep `just actions-lint` green.",
        "This repository has no actionlint gate of its own and is held with it so the",
        "org's repositories keep building on one runner image.",
        "Closes when: actionlint ships a release that recognises ubuntu-26.04.",
      ],
      matchDatasources: ["github-runners"],
      matchPackageNames: ["ubuntu"],
      allowedVersions: "<26",
    },
    {
      description: [
        "HOLDBACK HB-2026-003: TypeScript is held at 6.0.3.",
        '@typescript-eslint/eslint-plugin 8.70.1 declares `typescript: ">=4.8.4 <6.1.0"`',
        "and refuses to load on TypeScript 7. Same hold as openbunny/fiona.sm.",
        "Closes when: typescript-eslint releases with TypeScript 7 support.",
      ],
      matchPackageNames: ["typescript"],
      allowedVersions: "<6.1.0",
      groupName: "typescript holdback",
      automerge: false,
    },
    {
      description: [
        "HOLDBACK HB-2026-004: ESLint is held at 9.39.5.",
        "eslint-plugin-react 7.37.5, which arrives through eslint-config-next, declares",
        '`eslint: "^9.7"` and calls a rule-context API that ESLint 10 removed.',
        "Same hold as openbunny/fiona.sm.",
        "Closes when: eslint-plugin-react releases compatible with ESLint 10.",
      ],
      matchPackageNames: ["eslint"],
      allowedVersions: "<10.0.0",
      groupName: "eslint holdback",
      automerge: false,
    },
    {
      description: [
        "HOLDBACK HB-2026-005: eslint-plugin-unicorn is held at 65.x.",
        '66.0.0 and later declare `eslint: ">=10.4"`, which HB-2026-004 forbids, so',
        "taking unicorn alone would leave an unsatisfied peer range, not an upgrade.",
        "Same hold as openbunny/fiona.sm.",
        "Closes when: HB-2026-004 closes.",
      ],
      matchPackageNames: ["eslint-plugin-unicorn"],
      allowedVersions: "<66.0.0",
      groupName: "eslint-plugin-unicorn holdback",
      automerge: false,
    },
  ],
}
